// A refusal from a rule the diagnostic-code registry allocates NO number to.
//
// The assignment arm of the type checker's `type_mismatch` helper: its
// annotated-`let` sibling is PD0022, and this arm is judged as nothing at all.
// It is the subject of every NO_CODE control, read by BOTH of them —
// `tests/gi12_diagnostic_codes.rs` (`include_str!`) and the M3 mutant in
// `scripts/check-diagnostic-codes.sh` — so the two cannot drift into testing
// different programs. If a later unit codes this arm, both go red together.
//
// WHY IT LIVES HERE AND NOT UNDER tests/. `tests/` and `examples/` are the
// conformance roots, and every `.pd` under them must be a declared manifest
// row. This program is a control's SUBJECT, not a corpus fixture: declaring it
// would make it a reject row owed a code, which is the opposite of its job.
fn main() {
    let mut n: i64 = 1;
    n = 'a';
    print_int(n);
}
